"""The replay-occurrence classification table (frozen with the tools).

Every target occurrence (definition: tools/NAMING.md, "Target occurrences")
in the 49 Rust inputs of the pinned executable must match exactly one rule,
and every rule must match exactly its stated count. Both checkers fail
otherwise.

Rule: (file, item, region, token, ordinal, count, status, rw, purpose, lemmas)
  ordinal  an int (the n-th occurrence of that token in that item and region)
           or "*" (all of them; count must then equal the number found)
  rw       DECL | READ | WRITE | PATTERN | NONE  (Checker B derives this
           independently for code occurrences of `replays`, `last` and
           `.name` in model_tests.rs and must agree)
Semantic consumers are the rules whose status is in SEMANTIC.
"""

